 then % change in tensile modulus / tensile strength / length / weight.","at":"p. 45-46 Table 11","screens":true}],"category":"acid","verdict":"limited","screens":false},{"meaning":"Alkali resistance","items":[{"agent":"Strong bases","verdict":"not-resistant","text":"It is not suitable for service in strong acids, strong bases, or oxidizing agents. Thus, they are not recommended for uses outside of pH range 4–9.","source":"R-DUPONT-DELRIN-MODULE-III","id":"PB00286","conditions":null,"note":null,"at":"p. 43 Acids, Bases, and Oxidizing Agents","screens":true},{"agent":"Sodium Hydroxide, 10 %","verdict":"not-resistant","text":"U (unsatisfactory)","source":"R-DUPONT-DELRIN-MODULE-III","id":"PB00287","conditions":"365 days, 23 °C","note":"Delrin acetal homopolymer; Table 11 gives Conc. %, Duration (days), Temperature, then % change in tensile modulus / tensile strength / length / weight.","at":"p. 46 Table 11, Sodium Hydroxide","screens":true}],"category":"alkali","verdict":"not-resistant","screens":true},{"meaning":"Oil and grease resistance","items":[{"agent":"Hydrocarbons (gasolines, lubricants, hydraulic fluids)","verdict":"resistant","text":"Delrin acetal resin exhibits good dimensional stability and superior chemical resistance to the following: alcohols, aldehydes, esters, ethers, hydrocarbons (gasolines, lubricants, hydraulic fluids), agricultural chemicals, many weak acids and weak bases, water.","source":"R-DUPONT-DELRIN-MODULE-III","id":"PB00292","conditions":null,"note":null,"at":"p. 43 Chemical Resistance","screens":false},{"agent":"Gasolines (Exxon Regular)","verdict":"resistant","text":"Tensile strength of Delrin acetal resin is essentially unaffected by exposure to gasolines. Stiffness can be reduced a moderate amount, depending upon the concentration of aromatic hydrocarbons in the fuel. Exxon Regular: tensile modulus -12 %, tensile strength -4 %, length +0.2 %, weight +0.7 %","source":"R-DUPONT-DELRIN-MODULE-III","id":"PB00293","conditions":"820 days, 23 °C","note":"Delrin acetal homopolymer; Table 11 gives Conc. %, Duration (days), Temperature, then % change in tensile modulus / tensile strength / length / weight.","at":"p. 43 Gasolines; p. 47 Table 11 Gasolines","screens":false},{"agent":"Motor oil (Exxon \"Uniflo\" 10W30)","verdict":"resistant","text":"Tensile modulus +2 %, tensile strength +3 %, length -0.3 %, weight -0.2 % (\"Nujol\" mineral oil, 365 days, 23 °C: +10 / +1 / -0.1 / +0.3)","source":"R-DUPONT-DELRIN-MODULE-III","id":"PB00294","conditions":"365 days, 70 °C","note":"Delrin acetal homopolymer; Table 11 gives Conc. %, Duration (days), Temperature, then % change in tensile modulus / tensile strength / length / weight.","at":"p. 47 Table 11 Lubricants","screens":false}],"category":"oil-grease","verdict":"resistant","screens":false},{"meaning":"Water solubility","items":[{"agent":"Water","verdict":"resistant","text":"Delrin acetal resin exhibits good dimensional stability and superior chemical resistance to the following: ... many weak acids and weak bases, water.","source":"R-DUPONT-DELRIN-MODULE-III","id":"PB00295","conditions":null,"note":null,"at":"p. 43 Chemical Resistance","screens":false}],"category":"water-solubility","verdict":"resistant","screens":false},{"meaning":"Hydrolytic stability","items":[{"agent":"Steam or hot water, repeated use","verdict":"not-resistant","text":"The main property limitations are repeated use in steam or hot water, and exposure to strong acids or bases outside the pH range of 4–9.","source":"R-DUPONT-DELRIN-MODULE-III","id":"PB00296","conditions":null,"note":null,"at":"p. 5 Properties and Characteristics","screens":true}],"category":"hydrolysis","verdict":"not-resistant","screens":true},{"meaning":"Flammability","items":[{"agent":"UL 94 classification, all grades of Delrin","verdict":"not-resistant","text":"All grades of Delrin are classed as horizontal burning by Underwriters Laboratories (UL 94).","source":"R-DUPONT-DELRIN-MODULE-III","id":"PB00298","conditions":n